@startuml
'=============================================================================
' KIND      INTENDED -- a view of the process defined in
'           docs/development/engineering-system.md §4. That document is
'           normative; if this diagram and it disagree, the document wins.
' GROUNDING docs/development/engineering-system.md §4.1 (states), §4.2
'           (transition ownership), §4.2.1 (illegal transitions);
'           docs/decisions/ADR-0001-development-governance.md.
'
' Transition labels name the ACTOR who may perform them. That is the
' load-bearing content: a state machine whose edges anyone may take is
' not a governance model.
'
' This is the DEVELOPMENT work item. The RUNTIME work item is a different
' object with a different state machine -- see 07-inbox-item-state.puml.
'=============================================================================
!theme plain
title Learning Lab — development work-item states (INTENDED)

[*] --> Discovered

state Discovered
state Backlog as "Initiative / Backlog"
state Accepted as "Roundtable accepted"
state Roadmapped
state Ready
state Dispatched
state InProgress as "In progress"
state ManagerReview as "Manager review"
state Implemented
state Closed as "Roundtable closed"
state Parked
state Rejected
state Superseded

Discovered --> Backlog : **anyone** — written to intake\nwith its evidence

Backlog --> Accepted : **Roundtable** — it is real work
Backlog --> Parked : **Roundtable** — reason recorded
Backlog --> Rejected : **Roundtable** — reason recorded

Accepted --> Roadmapped : **Roundtable** — priority and\nroadmap placement decided

Roadmapped --> Ready : **Manager** — DoR satisfied

Ready --> Dispatched : **Manager** — bounded work order,\nWIP limit respected

Dispatched --> InProgress : **Coder** — work started

InProgress --> ManagerReview : **Coder** — implementation\n+ evidence returned

ManagerReview --> InProgress : **Manager** — rejected,\ncorrections required
ManagerReview --> Implemented : **Manager** — DoD satisfied

Implemented --> Closed : **Roundtable** — roadmap/architecture\nstatus updated from what landed

Closed --> Backlog : **Roundtable** — follow-up authorised\nas a NEW item
Parked --> Backlog : **Roundtable** — reactivated

Roadmapped --> Superseded : **Roundtable**
Closed --> [*]
Rejected --> [*]
Superseded --> [*]

note right of Ready
**DoR** — the item may not be dispatched
until unresolved policy is decided by
Roundtable rather than silently delegated
to the Coder.
end note

note right of Implemented
**Manager acceptance** answers:
"was the commissioned work implemented
correctly?"

It does not close roadmap authority, and
Manager may not take the next edge.
end note

note right of Closed
**Roundtable closure** answers:
"what does this result mean for the
roadmap, product and architecture?"

It is not a second code review.
end note

note as N1
**Always illegal** (engineering system §4.2.1)

  Discovered -> In progress          a finding became work with
                                     nobody deciding it should
  Roadmapped -> Dispatched           skips Ready; the Coder will
                                     invent policy while implementing
  Ready -> Implemented               no review happened
  Manager review -> Roundtable closed  collapses the two approvals
  Implemented -> Roundtable closed
    performed by Manager             Manager taking roadmap authority

If one of these appears to have happened, the work is out of process
and returns to the last legal state.
end note
@enduml
